] [17592186432499 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1f3bd7e4-e9ee-5ec1-b495-697d442c712e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432499 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}=2{b}_{1}+{b}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}=-{b}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express the $b$'s in terms of $c$'s. From the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=-{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=2(-{c}_{2})+{b}_{2}\\,⟹\\,{b}_{2}={c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}.\n$$\n\nSince $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write the vector $x$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-{b}_{1}+3{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-(-{c}_{2})+3({c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}) \\\\  & ={c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2} \\\\  & =7{c}_{2}+3{c}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432500 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432495 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432500 #edb/ref 1069 "q-34773" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432500 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432500 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where ${b}_{1}=4{c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=-2{c}_{1}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432500 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f3e71ae-af49-5472-af32-b57e5521039a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432500 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2} \\\\  & =-5{c}_{2}-3{c}_{1} \\\\  & =-5({c}_{2})+3(-{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}(4{c}_{2})+\\frac{3}{2}(-2{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{4}{b}_{1}+\\frac{3}{2}{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186432501 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432497 #edb/ref 1